From 8b813e3e3e37cce1824b8fda13c99f28162c7866 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nsbradley88 <3960699+nsbradley88@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 08:56:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 17/23] speculative: MTP draft-vocabulary subset
 (--spec-draft-vocab) for GLM5-Next

llama_set_draft_vocab() gathers the subset rows of the output head into a separate buffer of an MTP
draft context; the GLM5-Next MTP graph then computes only those rows and scatters them back to the full
vocabulary (get_rows by an inverse map, -inf outside the subset). The target verification is unchanged,
so the output stays exact; only drafts of out-of-subset tokens are lost.
--spec-draft-vocab FILE takes little-endian int32 token ids.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 37e8fcba01930199c223f52c2aa461ac3d6db373)
